      "writtenOn": "2024-10-10T21:04:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But Native code is depending on\n```\n  bool supports_msft_extensions() {\n    if (msft_.opcode.has_value()) {\n      return true;\n    }\n\n    uint16_t opcode \u003d hal_-\u003egetMsftOpcode();\n    if (opcode \u003d\u003d 0) {\n      return false;\n    }\n\n    msft_.opcode \u003d opcode;\n    log::info(\"MSFT opcode 0x{:04x}\", msft_.opcode.value());\n    return true;\n  }\n```\n\nI am not sure about the whole chain of call here, is it possible the native call  supports_msft_extensions, and it return true, while the SystemProperties isn\u0027t set ?\nIf we update `supports_msft_extensions` in native to check for the sysprop, wouldn\u0027t it be better ? (that what I mean by one source of truth)",
